# home-runtime-lib.manifest — the lib/ modules a self-contained agent home repo
# needs at runtime (PROJ-039/T-011 C2-v2.1c).
#
# This is the transitive import closure of the SHIPPED home-repo hook set's
# Python entry points — append-session-stop.py (Stop tasking), subagent-stop.py
# (SubagentStop), and session-end-finalise.py (SessionEnd: telemetry push →
# rollup → CST prune → session-finalise). The shell hooks import nothing from
# lib/. The finalise hook anchors the session-end lifecycle closure
# (telemetry_repo, cst_cleanup, session_finalise); its omission from the shipped
# hook set in C2-v2.1b is what dropped those three from this manifest (C2-v2.1c).
# scaffold.sh and sync-agent-tooling.sh copy ONLY these modules into a home
# repo's .claude/lib/ — NOT the whole 26-module agent-tooling lib/, which carries
# workstation/Hermes-only code (decay detector, one-shots, harnesses, reporting)
# that never runs inside a home repo.
#
# This list is enforced, not decorative: tests/proj039/test_home_runtime_lib_closure.py
# recomputes the closure from the shipped hooks and FAILS if it drifts from this
# manifest (a missing dependency, or a re-bloat module that nothing references).
# If you add/remove a lib import in a shipped hook, update this manifest and the
# test will confirm it matches.
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to agent-tooling/lib/. Blank lines and
# lines starting with '#' are ignored.

__init__.py
agent_identity.py
jsonl_scrape.py
qdrant_http.py
session_metadata.py
session_substrate.py
stop_telemetry.py
brief_substrate.py
work_items_extract.py
telemetry_repo.py
cst_cleanup.py
session_finalise.py
runtime_log.py
finalise_ledger.py
session_guard.py
lifecycle_mode.py
